course: dictionary
lesson: 2251
title: Cranky: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you need context to choose the right one. Read the words around cranky before you decide. «He's cranky because he missed his nap» tells you the child is bad-tempered. A tired child who has missed a sleep is easily annoyed.
explain: In a story, you might read about a cranky old neighbour. Cranky means grumpy here, because the word sits next to a person and their mood. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try your meaning in place of the word and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Cranky can also mean strange or odd, as in «cranky ideas». This meaning is mostly used in the UK. A cranky machine is different again: it is not working well. Check the clues in the sentence and you will know which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Cranky is an informal word, so you will hear it in everyday talk and stories more than in formal writing.
fact: «Cranky» means bad-tempered or easily annoyed, often because you are tired or hungry.
fact: In UK English, «cranky» can mean strange or odd, as in «cranky ideas».
fact: A cranky machine is one that is not working well or cannot be relied on.
fact: Similar words: grumpy, grouchy, crabby and ratty (UK) all describe someone who is cross or bad-tempered.
exercise: «He's cranky because he missed his nap.» What does cranky mean here? | *Bad-tempered and easily annoyed | Happy and excited | Strange and odd | Not working well
exercise: A UK friend says, «Those cranky ideas will never work.» What does cranky mean? | *Strange or odd | Bad-tempered and tired | Working perfectly | Very loud and noisy
exercise: The old printer is cranky and keeps jamming. What does cranky mean here? | Full of joy | *Not working well | Grumpy and rude | Very old and valuable
test: Which word is a synonym of cranky, meaning bad-tempered? | Generous | Silent | Huge | *Grumpy
test: Why is context useful when you meet cranky? | Context makes the word longer | Context means you never need to check a dictionary | Context tells you how to spell it | *Context shows which meaning fits
exam: Which sentence uses cranky to mean strange? | *«Her cranky idea about flying cats made us laugh.» | «The cranky printer keeps jamming.» | «He's cranky because he missed his nap.»
